CodeBrix patch 0013 - wgpuQueueGetNativeMetalCommandQueue returns the queue (wgpu-native/src/lib.rs)

WHAT: the Metal branch of wgpuQueueGetNativeMetalCommandQueue returns the queue's MTLCommandQueue
through wgpu-core's queue_as_hal and wgpu-hal's Queue::raw_queue (patches/0012) - borrowed, exactly
like wgpuDeviceGetNativeMetalDevice's MTLDevice - instead of logging a warning and returning NULL.
Off Metal it still returns NULL. wgpu.h's C API is unchanged.
WHY: SkiaSharp's Metal GRContext needs the device AND a command queue. With the WebGPU device's own
queue, Skia and WebGPU submit on one MTLCommandQueue and Metal orders their work, so the
CodeBrix.WebGpu.Skia owned route on macOS reaches ZeroCopy with no waits (SharesQueueWithSkia), as
it does on Vulkan and Direct3D 12. Fenced by the Skia tests that build a GRContext on a WebGPU device
(they skipped with "returned null" before), the Graphics MetalCommandQueue test, and the smoke test's
"MTLCommandQueue belongs to the device" check.
UPSTREAM: wgpu-native v29.0.1.1 returns NULL here with the comment "wgpu-hal v29 no longer exposes a
public accessor for the raw MTLCommandQueue. Return null until upstream adds one back." Drop this
patch (with 0012) when a vendored release returns the queue.

--- a/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
+++ b/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
@@ -3228,12 +3228,15 @@
     #[cfg(all(any(target_os = "ios", target_os = "macos"), feature = "metal"))]
     {
         let queue = queue.as_ref().expect("invalid queue");
-        // wgpu-hal v29 no longer exposes a public accessor for the raw
-        // MTLCommandQueue. Return null until upstream adds one back.
-        log::warn!(
-            "wgpuQueueGetNativeMetalCommandQueue: not available in current wgpu-hal version"
-        );
-        let _ = queue;
+        // CodeBrix (patches/0013): wgpu-hal v29 dropped the public accessor for the raw
+        // MTLCommandQueue; patches/0012 adds `raw_queue` back. Borrowed, like the device getter's.
+        let hal_queue = queue
+            .queue
+            .context
+            .queue_as_hal::<hal::api::Metal>(queue.queue.id);
+        if let Some(hal_queue) = hal_queue {
+            return hal_queue.raw_queue() as *const _ as *mut c_void;
+        }
         std::ptr::null_mut()
     }
     #[cfg(not(all(any(target_os = "ios", target_os = "macos"), feature = "metal")))]
